+        return Ok(lock);
+    }
+    // bd-05cda9: the lock already exists -- but an existing lock is NOT
+    // necessarily a LIVE sync. A `caco file sync` that hung (e.g. on a broken
+    // SSH key) and was killed mid-hold leaves a STALE lock that blocks EVERY
+    // future sync forever (the observed ~4h fleet-wide file-cache wedge: holder
